      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "209e5e23-9e2c-532a-a8f6-98ab591ff0e4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Inter-Allied Socialist Conferences of World War I, First World War, Hoboken Docks Fire\n- Organizations: socialist parties of the Entente or Allied powers\n- Countries/Blocs: Allies of World War I, Entente Powers, Central Powers\n- Vessels: SS Main\n- Places: Bremen, Baltimore\n\nFacts:\n- During the First World War, a number of Inter-Allied Socialist Conferences were held by the socialist parties of the Entente or Allied powers.\n- The Allies of World War I, also called the Entente Powers, were the countries that opposed the Central Powers in the First World War.\n- SS Main was launched in 1900 and served on the route from Bremen to Baltimore.\n- SS Main was involved in the 1900 Hoboken Docks Fire.\n- SS Main remained in service on the Bremen to Baltimore route until the Allies of World War I seized her in 1914.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "d277a053-c302-58c7-9cde-c2d6aed5434b",
        "text": "Page: Inter-Allied Socialist Conferences of World War I. Sentence: During the First World War there were a number of conferences of the socialist parties of the Entente or Allied powers.\nPage: Allies of World War I. Sentence: The Allies of World War I, or Entente Powers, were the countries that opposed the Central Powers in the First World War.\nPage: SS Main (1900). Sentence: She was in service on the route from Bremen to Baltimore from her 1900 launch until seized by the Allies of World War I in 1914, and was involved in the 1900 Hoboken Docks Fire.",
